    <comment>New package comfyui for openSUSE:Factory from science:machinelearning (ComfyUI cone). pluskalm is the science:machinelearning package maintainer.

Requires python-av &gt;= 16 (Factory is 14.2.0 until sr#1372737). python-comfy-angle is Recommends only and is not packaged (prebuilt Electron libEGL/libGLESv2).

INTERDEPENDENT REQUESTS - please stage together (ComfyUI cone):
  * sr#1372780 python-trampoline
  * sr#1372737 python-av (devel:languages:python; Factory 14.2.0, need &gt;= 16 for comfyui)
  * remaining cone packages from science:machinelearning being submitted in this batch

Fri Aug 21 09:01:47 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal &lt;mpluskal@suse.com&gt;

- Initial package of ComfyUI 0.33.3: node-graph engine for local
  image, video, audio and 3D generation
  * Single-flavour application: tree in /usr/share/comfyui,
    launcher /usr/bin/comfyui
  * Launcher defaults --base-directory and --database-url to
    $XDG_DATA_HOME/comfyui (or ~/.local/share/comfyui)
  * Already includes the 0.28.0 security fixes:
    CVE-2026-56670, CVE-2026-56671, CVE-2026-56672, CVE-2026-56673
</comment>
    <requestid>1372800</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="2">
    <srcmd5>f130a4f7c763cde2239aeb759b0e2cc4</srcmd5>
    <version>0.33.3</version>
    <time>1787427337</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>- Fix the very first start of comfyui aborting with a
  FileNotFoundError instead of serving the web UI: add
  comfyui-create-custom-nodes-directory.patch, which creates the
  custom_nodes directory in the per-user base directory
- Load the custom nodes shipped with ComfyUI again: the per-user
  base directory had hidden them, so SaveImageWebsocket, used by
  the packaged websocket API example, was unavailable
- Do not create the per-user directory tree for comfyui --help
- Require python-comfyui-frontend-package 1.50.6 (XSS fixes
  GHSA-2gr5-vw2p-2hcf, GHSA-j6xv-rx8r-mh6j, GHSA-8xxc-66vh-2pf3)

Supersedes sr#1373017, which carried only the Requires bump.

The FileNotFoundError is already live in Factory (comfyui-0.33.3-2.1):
os.listdir() on a per-user custom_nodes directory that nothing creates,
so every first-time user hits it on first start and it does not
self-heal. Fixed in folder_paths.py rather than the launcher so that
--base-directory and direct main.py invocations are covered too.

INTERDEPENDENT: please stage together with
python-comfyui-frontend-package 1.50.6 (sr#1373016). ComfyUI 0.33.3
pinned the frontend at 1.49.6; Factory cannot replace that RPM without
this Requires bump. sr#1373016 is currently in
openSUSE:Factory:Staging:adi:28 and needs to be re-paired with this
request.</comment>
    <requestid>1373109</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="3">
    <srcmd5>7cc77b3eb32e94613ad07d8acd7a07fa</srcmd5>
    <version>0.33.3</version>
    <time>1787579030</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Start on the CPU when no accelerator is present

comfy/model_management.py assumes a GPU unless --cpu is passed: cpu_state
is set to GPU at import and only args.cpu ever sets it back. On a
CPU-only machine the module level

  total_vram = get_total_memory(get_torch_device())

then raises &quot;AssertionError: Torch not compiled with CUDA enabled&quot; while
ComfyUI is still importing, so the server never starts. Factory builds
PyTorch without CUDA and without ROCm, so this is what every user gets
unless they know about --cpu.

Patch1 falls back to the CPU device when none of the accelerator
backends the module already probes is available. It logs a warning
rather than an informational line on purpose: the same condition holds
for a GPU-capable PyTorch whose device is momentarily unusable, and a
silent CPU run there would be far slower than expected.

Also bumps the exact python-comfy-aimdo requirement to 0.4.14 to match
request 1373273, so the pin keeps resolving when that lands.

Verified by running the built rpm, since neither the ComfyUI nor the
comfy-aimdo %check reaches this code: in an x86_64 container with the
Factory CPU-only torch, a flagless start from a clean home now reaches
&quot;Starting server&quot; instead of exiting 1.</comment>
    <requestid>1373274</requestid>
  </revision>
